---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { ChatWindowPlayground } from '../../components/ChatWindowDemo';
---

<Docs
  title="Chat Window"
  description="A chat that opens from a corner launcher over any page, and switches to a side drawer or a full page."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Chat Window</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The frame for a quick chat that opens over any page without leaving it. It holds a header, your chat, and a message
    box. Switch it to a side drawer or a full page, or minimize it back into its launcher. The page behind stays usable
    the whole time.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="chat-window-demo">
    <ChatWindowPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Chat Window usage"
      code={`import {
  ChatWindow,
  ChatWindowActions,
  ChatWindowBody,
  ChatWindowClose,
  ChatWindowContent,
  ChatWindowFooter,
  ChatWindowHeader,
  ChatWindowLauncher,
  ChatWindowLayoutMenu,
  ChatWindowTitle,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chat-window";

<ChatWindow open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} layout={layout} onLayoutChange={setLayout}>
  <ChatWindowLauncher>
    <AgentAvatar agentId="bud" name="Bud" size="sm" />
    Bud
  </ChatWindowLauncher>
  <ChatWindowContent>
    <ChatWindowHeader>
      <ChatWindowTitle>Late supplier deliveries</ChatWindowTitle>
      <ChatWindowActions>
        <ChatWindowLayoutMenu />
        <ChatWindowClose />
      </ChatWindowActions>
    </ChatWindowHeader>
    <ChatWindowBody>
      <MessageScrollerProvider>…</MessageScrollerProvider>
    </ChatWindowBody>
    <ChatWindowFooter>
      <ChatInput … />
    </ChatWindowFooter>
  </ChatWindowContent>
</ChatWindow>`}
    />
    <p>
      Chat Window is only the frame. Put your existing chat in it: a <code>MessageScroller</code> in{' '}
      <code>ChatWindowBody</code> and a <code>ChatInput</code> in <code>ChatWindowFooter</code>. It works controlled
      with <code>open</code> and <code>layout</code>, or uncontrolled with <code>defaultOpen</code> and{' '}
      <code>defaultLayout</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Layouts</h2>
    <p>
      <code>layout</code> is <code>"window"</code> (default), <code>"drawer"</code>, or <code>"page"</code>. A window
      floats in its corner at 34rem by 44rem and shrinks to fit. A drawer is 28rem wide and fills the height of the
      corner's side. A full page covers the viewport and keeps the thread and message box in a 48rem column. Below 640px
      every layout fills the screen, so the menu offers only Full page and Minimize.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your chat stays mounted while the window is minimized, so drafts, scroll position, and a running reply survive.
      Set <code>keepMounted={'{false}'}</code> on <code>ChatWindowContent</code> to unmount it instead.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Open the full chat page</h2>
    <p>
      If your app has its own chat page, go there when someone picks Full page, and leave the layout as it was. When
      they come back, the window is where they left it.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Full page opens a route"
      code={`<ChatWindow
  open={open}
  onOpenChange={setOpen}
  layout={layout}
  onLayoutChange={next => {
    if (next === "page") navigate(\`/chat/\${chatId}\`);
    else setLayout(next);
  }}
>`}
    />
    <p>
      To offer fewer layouts, pass them to the menu:{' '}
      <code>{'<ChatWindowLayoutMenu layouts={["window", "page"]} />'}</code>.<code>labels</code> renames any item, and{' '}
      <code>showMinimize={'{false}'}</code> removes Minimize.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Corners and your own launcher</h2>
    <p>
      <code>corner</code> is <code>"bottom-right"</code> (default), <code>"bottom-left"</code>, <code>"top-right"</code>
      , or <code>"top-left"</code>. The launcher and window sit in that corner, the window grows out of it, and a drawer
      fills that side. <code>ChatWindowLauncher</code> is an outline pill that hides while the window is open. To open
      the window from a header button or a draggable launcher of your own, use <code>ChatWindowTrigger</code> with{' '}
      <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      To keep the window inside one region of the page, as this demo does, pass that region as <code>container</code>{' '}
      and give it <code>contain: layout</code>. The window and launcher then sit in the region's corner instead of the
      viewport's.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="chat-window-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ChatWindow</code> wraps a non-modal Base UI dialog and takes its props, plus <code>layout</code>,{' '}
      <code>defaultLayout</code>, <code>onLayoutChange</code>, and <code>corner</code>. It always sets{' '}
      <code>modal={'{false}'}</code> and ignores clicks outside, so the window only closes from its own controls or
      Escape.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ChatWindowContent</code> takes <code>keepMounted</code> (default <code>true</code>), <code>container</code>,
      and every Base UI popup prop. It sets <code>data-slot="chat-window-content"</code>, <code>data-layout</code>, and{' '}
      <code>data-corner</code>. <code>ChatWindowHeader</code>, <code>ChatWindowActions</code>,{' '}
      <code>ChatWindowBody</code>, and <code>ChatWindowFooter</code> render a <code>div</code> and accept{' '}
      <code>render</code>. <code>ChatWindowTitle</code> renders an <code>h2</code>. Inside a breadcrumb, wrap only the
      current page and pass <code>{'render={<span />}'}</code>. <code>ChatWindowClose</code> takes <code>label</code>{' '}
      (default <code>"Close"</code>).
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The window has <code>role="dialog"</code> and is named by <code>ChatWindowTitle</code>. It does not trap focus or
      hide the page, so people can keep working beside it. When it opens, focus goes to the window itself, so the
      composer shows no focus ring and no phone keyboard pops up until someone clicks or tabs into it. Pass{' '}
      <code>initialFocus</code> to focus something else. Escape, Minimize, and Close return focus to the launcher. The
      layout button's name includes the current layout, and every icon button has a tooltip.
    </p>
    <p>
      A window grows from its corner and fades in over 180ms, and shrinks back in 120ms. A drawer slides 2.5rem from its
      side. Motion turns off when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Chat Window uses <code>--sprout-canvas</code> for the window's frame, <code>--sprout-surface</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>. Set{' '}
      <code>--sprout-chat-window-width</code>, <code>-height</code>, <code>-drawer-width</code>, <code>-measure</code>,
      and <code>-inset</code> on <code>:root</code> to change its size and distance from the corner.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
